;;; A `(solve :hypothesis-relations …)` list that names a relation the program
;;; does not have loads, and leaves H empty —
;;; M1f **W76**, register row `W76/hypothesis-relations`, filed by S1f.7.8 (T1f.7.8.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The program's relation is `likes`, and its `(solve …)` writes `like`. With
;;; the name spelt right, `(solve :hypothesis-relations (likes))`: H is the two
;;; candidates of `likes`, `(likes Ann Red)` and `(likes Red Ann)`, and R is four
;;; states.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The program names no relation `like` outside the list: the program is
;;; refused at load, at the `like`, one line, on every command (exit 1,
;;; `ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `63f1e569`, release: The program loads. No relation is in the list, so H
;;; is empty and R is {∅}, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.8 (T1f.7.8.3).

(relation likes Person Color :why "{?1} likes {?2}")
(rule glad ()
  :match  (likes ?p ?c)
  :assert (glad ?p)
  :why "{?p} likes {?c}, so {?p} is glad")
(is-a Ann Person) (is-a Red Color)
(solve :hypothesis-relations (like))
